  "observation": "Three guarded original captures compare 2921 extended-prefix PC increments, 993 pending fe/a2 music waits, 35 music polls and 35 caller commits. The polls cover selectors 12 and 6, with nine and 24 pending returns followed by completion at frontend runs 591 and 1601. Two complete source SMDS files, 5900 bytes total, match original consumer inputs and are followed by sequence creation/backlinks and start calls. The first 8192-byte block of the selected 168000-byte WDS matches the original wave-stream input. All captures preserve the control outputs exactly.",
  "interpretation": "The original gate at 0x8004f308 is the field music-poll result. Pending fe/a2 retries its prefix and requests a break without changing budget mode. The earlier initialization safeguard permits those 993 waits to continue. Music poll state separates wave transfer, deferred sequence reads, disc completion and sequence start. These loading states constrain native media services but do not establish player readiness or gameplay cadence.",
  "confidence": "supported",
  "validation": {
    "preconditions": [
      "Use the exact selected Disc 1 raw track, executable and field overlay; source-check.json rechecks the raw SHA against the previous verified source audit.",
      "Use the pinned Nix observation-trace shell and the authored field23-entry-dialogue cold-boot route. Capture each group with its original code guards and bounded memory."
    ],
    "commands": [
      "python tools/analysis/verify_media_ready.py prepare --raw .local/references/source-1/disc.bin --profile na-slus-00664-39c547a9afc6 --map 23 --group events --output <new-private-spec>",
      "python tools/reference/scenario.py tests/reference-inputs/field23-entry-dialogue.json --content \"discs/Xenogears disc 1.chd\" --trace-instructions <spec> --output <new-private-run>",
      "python tools/analysis/verify_media_ready.py compare --raw .local/references/source-1/disc.bin --profile na-slus-00664-39c547a9afc6 --map 23 --group events --capture <run>/capture --output <new-private-comparison>",
      "Repeat prepare/capture/compare for groups poll and resources.",
      "python -m unittest tests.test_event_media tests.test_music_loading",
      "env PYTHONPATH=. python .local/analysis/phase1-media-ready-20260908/audit.py (choose new private output names on reproduction)"
    ],
    "expected": "Exact reconstructed PC, controls, captured music state, return values and caller commit; complete selected sequence input identity and bounded wave-prefix identity. Reject missing/altered evidence, qualify source/trace hashes and preserve original control outputs.",
    "actual": "All three source-qualified comparisons pass, with zero guard mismatches, unavailable ranges, budget exhaustion or trace failure. Twenty-one original-input corruptions are rejected. Six sequence read/create/start operations correlate across captures. All three runs match full RAM, external state, audio and 18 PNGs. Both earlier conditional windows and all three event-state groups pass with the current extended decoder.",
    "result": "passed",
    "tolerance": "Exact 256-byte actor prefix plus 196 global bytes for a2, exact captured prefix state, exact 196 poll/global bytes and u32 result, exact 5900 sequence bytes, and exact initial 8192 WDS bytes by digest. Other service state and playback are unvalidated.",
